CORE
division.c
--evaluation-order-check --div-by-zero-check
^--evaluation-order-check has no effect on goto binaries; pass it to goto-cc when compiling them$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[.*evaluation-order
--
Passing --evaluation-order-check to cbmc does not affect goto binaries, which
goto-cc has already converted in one fixed evaluation order; cbmc warns about
this. In this fixed order, f() executes before a / b, so the division by zero
that occurs when a / b is evaluated first is not found (see division.desc for
the result when the option is passed to goto-cc). The fixed order of the
operands of + does not depend on the target, unlike the order of function
call arguments.
